{%- comment -%}
  Future Basics Make — v4. The Design Lab leads, production by Future Basics follows:
    01 · design lab        — the six ways to design and every product type (real screens from the Lab)
    02 · the tech pack     — spec sheet, checklist, factory sign-off, and the tools by subscription (pricing)
    03 · made by us        — minimums and lead times per category, how it gets made
    systems                — lives in sections/make-systems.liquid, between the two halves
  The 'part' setting splits this section around it: one instance shows hero → made by us, another questions → close.
  Its styles are in assets/make-v4.css (assets-make-v4.css here).
  Screenshots of the Design Lab are served by the hub (hub.thefuturebasics.com/help/assets/make-*.webp), taken from the live Lab.
  Primary CTA opens the Design Lab (hub.thefuturebasics.com/join?for=lab); the free tech pack is /start; production goes to /pages/contact.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign start_url = section.settings.start_url | default: 'https://hub.thefuturebasics.com/start'
  assign contact_url = section.settings.cta_url | default: '/pages/contact'
  assign shots = 'https://hub.thefuturebasics.com/help/assets/'
  assign lab_url = section.settings.lab_url | default: 'https://hub.thefuturebasics.com/join?for=lab'
  assign marks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'mark'
  assign figures = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'figure'
  assign objects = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'object'
  assign projects = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'project'
  assign steps = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'step'
  assign questions = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'question'
  assign part = section.settings.part | default: 'all'
-%}

{{ 'make-v4.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div class="mk3">

  {%- unless part == 'end' -%}
  <section class="mk3__hero mk3__pad">
    <div>
      <span class="mk3__mono">future basics · make</span>
      <h1>{{ section.settings.hero_title | default: 'design it yourself.' }} <span>{{ section.settings.hero_accent | default: 'we make it properly.' }}</span></h1>
      <div class="mk3__lede">{{ section.settings.hero_lede | default: '<p>The Design Lab is the studio we use on every project, now open to you. <b>Describe it, pick it from a menu, start from a sketch, draw it from scratch, plan a whole line or bring a photo.</b> Every way ends in a tech pack a factory can make from, for clothes, headwear, bags, footwear, plush, toys and electronics. Then Future Basics makes it.</p>' }}</div>
      <div class="mk3__actions">
        <a class="mk3__btn" href="{{ lab_url }}&utm_source=thefuturebasics&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=make_hero">open the design lab</a>
        <a class="mk3__btn mk3__btn--ghost" href="{{ start_url }}?utm_source=thefuturebasics&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=make_hero">start a tech pack <i>free</i></a>
      </div>
      <p class="mk3__fine">design lab $499 for 90 days · membership $100/month · first tech pack free</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mk3__device">
      <div class="mk3__phone"><img src="{{ shots }}make-phone-recipe.webp" alt="The Design Lab's recipe menu on a phone: a pullover hoodie picked, with a zip pocket and cropped added" width="1100" height="1893" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"></div>
      <span class="mk3__tag mk3__tag--a">6 ways to design</span>
      <span class="mk3__tag mk3__tag--b">every product type</span>
      <span class="mk3__tag mk3__tag--c">factory-ready tech pack</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- if marks.size > 0 -%}
  <section class="mk3__marks mk3__pad" aria-label="Brands we have made product with">
    <span class="mk3__mono">{{ section.settings.marks_label | default: 'made with' }}</span>
    <ul>{%- for b in marks -%}<li {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>{{ b.settings.name }}</li>{%- endfor -%}</ul>
  </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ───────── 01 · ways to design ───────── {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="mk3__pad" id="design-lab">
    <div class="mk3__half">
      <div><span class="mk3__mono">01 · the design lab</span><h2>six ways in. <span>one tech pack out.</span></h2></div>
      <p><b>Design it whichever way suits you.</b> Every way in opens in the same Studio, becomes measured flats, a pattern or 3D parts, and ends in a tech pack a factory can quote and make from. These are real screens from the Lab.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mk3__ways">
      <article class="mk3__way"><div class="mk3__way-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-way-ai.webp" alt="The New design window: a boxy heavyweight hoodie described in a few words, three concepts to draw" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__way-body"><span class="mk3__mono">with ai</span><h3>describe it.</h3><p>A few words are enough. Three concepts come back, each checked against what inspired it, ready to open in the Studio.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__way"><div class="mk3__way-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-way-recipe.webp" alt="The recipe menu: a button-up shirt with a flap pocket and button-down collar, drawn in the Workwear colours" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__way-body"><span class="mk3__mono">by recipe</span><h3>order it like a meal.</h3><p>Pick one of 26 bases, add pockets, zips and collars from 31 add-ons, and choose a colour system. The flat redraws with every tap.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__way"><div class="mk3__way-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-way-sketch.webp" alt="The sketch pack with a boxy cropped tee open in tobacco canvas" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__way-body"><span class="mk3__mono">from a sketch</span><h3>start from a real flat.</h3><p>Pick one of 382 professional flat sketches, choose its cloth and colour, and it opens in the Studio with both in place.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__way"><div class="mk3__way-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-way-scratch.webp" alt="A blank page in the Studio with a t-shirt outline as a guide" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__way-body"><span class="mk3__mono">from scratch</span><h3>draw it yourself.</h3><p>A blank page with the product’s outline as a guide, at real size. Draw with a pen tool or an Apple Pencil; the flats and pattern follow.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__way"><div class="mk3__way-img"><img src="{{ shots }}lab-plan.jpg" alt="A line plan: six pieces, a median price, a blended margin and the units" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__way-body"><span class="mk3__mono">a whole line</span><h3>plan a season.</h3><p>Describe a season or a drop. The assistant drafts the pieces with target prices, landed cost and margin, then concepts for each.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__way"><div class="mk3__way-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-way-photo.webp" alt="The free tech pack page: add a design, sketch or photo and get a draft tech pack" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__way-body"><span class="mk3__mono">from a photo</span><h3>bring any image.</h3><p>A render, a sketch, a photo of a sample or a screenshot becomes a draft tech pack in minutes, with callouts pinned to it. The first one is free.</p></div></article>
    </div>
    <ol class="mk3__flow" aria-label="Where every way in leads">
      <li><span>any way in</span></li><li><span>the studio</span></li><li><span>flats, pattern or 3d parts</span></li><li><span>tech pack</span></li><li><span>factory sign-off</span></li><li><span>made by future basics</span></li>
    </ol>

    <div class="mk3__sub"><h3>every product type</h3><span class="mk3__mono">its own tools for each</span></div>
    <div class="mk3__types">
      <article class="mk3__type mk3__type--wide"><div class="mk3__type-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-type-apparel.webp" alt="Flat drawings of a tee, hoodie, shirt, bomber, trousers, dress, coat and skirt from the Design Lab" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__type-body"><h3>apparel</h3><p>Tops and jersey, knitwear, outerwear, tailoring, bottoms, dresses and sets: measured flats, front and back, graded across the size run.</p><b>from 50 pcs · 8–14 wks</b></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__type"><div class="mk3__type-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-type-headwear.webp" alt="A cap, bucket hat and beanie drawn in the Design Lab" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__type-body"><h3>headwear</h3><p>Six-panel caps, bucket hats and beanies, drawn and measured like the rest.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__type"><div class="mk3__type-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-type-bags.webp" alt="A tote bag drawn in the Design Lab" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__type-body"><h3>bags</h3><p>Totes, backpacks and small bags, with the pockets and handles where they go.</p></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__type"><div class="mk3__type-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-type-footwear.webp" alt="A sneaker in the Design Lab drawn from the outside, inside, top and bottom" width="1200" height="843" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__type-body"><h3>footwear</h3><p>A parametric last, the upper flattened off it into pattern pieces, a full size run, and tech flats from four sides.</p><b>6–12 month programme</b></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__type"><div class="mk3__type-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-type-plush.webp" alt="A plush bear in the Design Lab drawn from the front, back and side" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__type-body"><h3>plush</h3><p>Your character, patterned piece by piece like clothing, with a photo-real picture drawn from the pattern.</p><b>from 300 pcs · 10–16 wks</b></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__type"><div class="mk3__type-img"><img src="{{ shots }}make-type-electronics.webp" alt="A round speaker in the Design Lab as numbered 3D parts with a unit cost and tooling" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><div class="mk3__type-body"><h3>toys, objects + electronics</h3><p>Real 3D parts in an exploded view, with materials, tooling, unit cost, a bill of materials, and STL and STEP files.</p><b>tooling-dependent</b></div></article>
      <article class="mk3__type mk3__type--text"><div class="mk3__type-body"><span class="mk3__mono">and more</span><h3>home + accessories</h3><p>Blankets, objects for a room, belts, socks and small goods: start from scratch or describe it, and it ends in a tech pack like everything else.</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ───────── 02 · the tech pack + pricing ───────── {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="mk3__platform mk3__pad" id="tech-pack">
    <div class="mk3__half">
      <div><span class="mk3__mono">02 · the tech pack</span><h2>everything a factory needs. <span>nothing it doesn’t.</span></h2></div>
      <p><b>The tech pack is where every way in arrives.</b> A checklist shows what is left before it is ready, and the spec sheet is the document a sample room works from, in inches with centimetres alongside.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mk3__feat">
      <div class="mk3__shot"><img src="{{ shots }}make-pack-spec.webp" alt="A spec sheet from the Design Lab: front and back flats of a cropped hoodie and its points of measure graded from XS to XXL" width="1800" height="1210" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="mk3__feat-copy"><span class="mk3__mono">spec sheet</span><h3>a real document, not a moodboard.</h3><p>Front and back flats, placements in inches, colour and stitching, and points of measure graded across the size run.</p>
        <ul><li>Points of measure from XS to XXL, with tolerances</li><li>Colourways with Pantone C codes, matched from the colour itself</li><li>A bill of materials from the fabrics, trims and labels you choose</li><li>A cost estimate, private to you: landed cost, margin and price breaks</li><li>PDF and Excel export</li></ul></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mk3__feat">
      <div class="mk3__shot"><img src="{{ shots }}make-pack-checklist.webp" alt="The Studio's checklist before the tech pack: the flats saved, it can be made as drawn, the main fabric still to choose" width="1340" height="1005" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="mk3__feat-copy"><span class="mk3__mono">checklist</span><h3>you always know what is left.</h3><p>Seven checks stand between a design and its tech pack, each with a button to finish it. “Can be made as drawn” is checked for you as you design.</p>
        <ul><li>The concept picture, drawn from the flats in one tap</li><li>Graphics placed, the flats saved, the main fabric chosen</li><li>A make check that flags what a factory cannot sew</li><li>Approved, then sent to the tech pack</li></ul></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mk3__feat">
      <div class="mk3__shot"><img src="{{ shots }}05-callouts.jpg" alt="A tech pack's callouts pinned on a sneaker: each detail numbered with its spec" width="1280" height="860" loading="lazy"></div>
      <div class="mk3__feat-copy"><span class="mk3__mono">factory sign-off</span><h3>the factory signs every detail.</h3><p>The factory works from a private link in its own language and acknowledges every callout before anything is cut. Then we make it.</p>
        <ul><li>The factory’s copy in Chinese, Spanish, Portuguese or Italian</li><li>You approve, Future Basics signs, the factory countersigns</li><li>v1 stays live while v2 is edited; signed versions lock</li><li>A pack sent to a factory carries the spec only: no retail price and no unit costs</li></ul></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mk3__sub" id="pricing" style="border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.3)"><h3>the tools, by subscription</h3><span class="mk3__mono">no retainer · cancel anytime</span></div>
    <div class="mk3__prices" style="margin-top:0">
      <div class="mk3__price mk3__price--lab"><span class="mk3__mono">design lab</span><b>$499<small>/90 days</small></b><p>All six ways in, every product type, the Studio and the libraries in your own room. 40 AI generations included, then $2.50 each. Tech packs included while it is open.</p><a href="{{ lab_url }}&utm_source=thefuturebasics&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=make_pricing">open the design lab →</a></div>
      <div class="mk3__price"><span class="mk3__mono">studio membership</span><b>$100<small>/month</small></b><p>Unlimited tech packs, versions and factory links for your studio. Cancel anytime.</p></div>
      <div class="mk3__price"><span class="mk3__mono">per pack</span><b>$48</b><p>One tech pack from an image, with a cost estimate, PDF and Excel, Future Basics review and the factory’s copy in its language.</p></div>
      <div class="mk3__price mk3__price--hot"><span class="mk3__mono">first pack</span><b>free</b><p>Your first tech pack from an image, start to finish. No card needed.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="mk3__compare">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">getting a product designed</th><th scope="col">cost</th><th scope="col">time</th><th scope="col">factory-ready</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>freelance designer + technical designer</td><td>$300–800 a pack, plus design</td><td>1–3 weeks</td><td>email and PDFs</td></tr>
          <tr><td>design software + PLM</td><td>$10,000+ a year</td><td>weeks to set up</td><td>yes, if the factory logs in</td></tr>
          <tr class="us"><td>future basics design lab</td><td>$499 for 90 days, or $100 a month</td><td>an afternoon</td><td>private link, every callout signed</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="mk3__actions">
      <a class="mk3__btn" href="{{ lab_url }}&utm_source=thefuturebasics&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=make_lab">open the design lab</a>
      <a class="mk3__btn mk3__btn--ghost" href="{{ start_url }}?utm_source=thefuturebasics&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=make_lab">start your free tech pack</a>
      <a class="mk3__btn mk3__btn--ghost" href="https://hub.thefuturebasics.com/pricing">see pricing</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ───────── 03 · made by future basics ───────── {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="mk3__pad" id="experience">
    <div class="mk3__half">
      <div><span class="mk3__mono">03 · made by future basics</span><h2>you design it. <span>we make it.</span></h2></div>
      <p><b>Whatever you design in the Lab, Future Basics can make.</b> Send us the tech pack and we take it from there: sampling, production, quality control and delivery, at a landed cost you can see. Cut-and-sew, not printed blanks. Every category below has a real minimum and a real lead time.</p>
    </div>

    {%- if figures.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="mk3__figures">
      {%- for b in figures -%}<div class="mk3__figure" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}><b>{{ b.settings.figure }}</b><span>{{ b.settings.label }}</span></div>{%- endfor -%}
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if projects.size > 0 or request.design_mode -%}
    <div class="mk3__sub"><h3>selected work</h3><span class="mk3__mono">{{ projects.size }} project{% if projects.size != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span></div>
    {%- if projects.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="mk3__projects">
      {%- for b in projects -%}
      <article class="mk3__project" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>
        <div class="mk3__project-img">{%- if b.settings.image != blank -%}{{ b.settings.image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: widths: '360, 540, 720, 900', sizes: '(max-width: 620px) 100vw, (max-width: 1000px) 50vw, 33vw', loading: 'lazy', alt: b.settings.image.alt | default: b.settings.title }}{%- endif -%}</div>
        <div class="mk3__project-body">
          {%- if b.settings.client != blank -%}<span class="mk3__mono">{{ b.settings.client }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          <h3>{{ b.settings.title }}</h3>
          {%- if b.settings.body != blank -%}<p>{{ b.settings.body }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          <div class="mk3__chips">{%- if b.settings.category != blank -%}<span>{{ b.settings.category }}</span>{%- endif -%}{%- if b.settings.quantity != blank -%}<span>{{ b.settings.quantity }}</span>{%- endif -%}{%- if b.settings.lead_time != blank -%}<span>{{ b.settings.lead_time }}</span>{%- endif -%}</div>
        </div>
      </article>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
    {%- else -%}
    <p class="mk3__empty">Add “Project” blocks in the theme editor: an image, the client, what it was, quantity and lead time. This note only shows in the editor.</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if objects.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="mk3__sub"><h3>minimums and lead times</h3><span class="mk3__mono">per style</span></div>
    <div class="mk3__cats">
      {%- for b in objects -%}
      <div class="mk3__cat{% if b.settings.is_note %} mk3__cat--note{% endif %}" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>
        <span class="mk3__mono">{{ b.settings.cap }}</span>
        <h3>{{ b.settings.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ b.settings.body }}</p>
        {%- if b.settings.moq != blank -%}<b>{{ b.settings.moq }}</b>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if steps.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="mk3__sub"><h3>how it gets made</h3><span class="mk3__mono">lab to delivery</span></div>
    <ol class="mk3__steps">
      {%- for b in steps -%}<li class="mk3__step" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}><span class="mk3__mono">{{ b.settings.key }}</span><h3>{{ b.settings.title }}</h3><p>{{ b.settings.body }}</p>{%- if b.settings.note != blank -%}<em>{{ b.settings.note }}</em>{%- endif -%}</li>{%- endfor -%}
    </ol>
    {%- endif -%}


  </section>



  {%- endunless -%}

  {%- unless part == 'top' -%}
  {%- if questions.size > 0 -%}
  <section class="mk3__faq mk3__pad" id="faq">
    <div><span class="mk3__mono">questions</span><h2>the honest answers.</h2></div>
    <div>
      {%- for b in questions -%}<details {{ b.shopify_attributes }}><summary>{{ b.settings.title }}</summary><p>{{ b.settings.body }}</p></details>{%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  <section class="mk3__close mk3__pad">
    <div class="mk3__door mk3__door--self">
      <div><span class="mk3__mono">do it yourself</span><h2>open the design lab.</h2></div>
      <p>Six ways to design and every product type, ending in a tech pack a factory can make from. $499 for 90 days, or start from any image: your first tech pack is free.</p>
      <div class="mk3__actions" style="margin-top:0"><a class="mk3__btn" href="{{ lab_url }}&utm_source=thefuturebasics&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=make_close">open the design lab</a><a class="mk3__btn mk3__btn--ghost" href="{{ start_url }}?utm_source=thefuturebasics&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=make_close">free tech pack</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="mk3__door">
      <div><span class="mk3__mono">then we make it</span><h2>send us the tech pack.</h2></div>
      <p>Sampling, production, quality control and delivery, from fifty pieces, at a landed cost you can see.</p>
      <a class="mk3__btn mk3__btn--ghost" href="{{ contact_url }}">talk to us about production</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="mk3__foot mk3__pad"><span class="mk3__mono">future basics · a non-linear progress corp®</span><span class="mk3__mono">product development + software + commerce systems</span></footer>
  {%- endunless -%}
</div>

{%- if section.settings.faq_schema and questions.size > 0 and part != 'top' -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{%- for b in questions -%}{"@type":"Question","name":{{ b.settings.title | json }},"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":{{ b.settings.body | json }}}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}]}
</script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Make — design lab",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_url", "label": "Start a project link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "start_url", "label": "Tech pack start link", "default": "https://hub.thefuturebasics.com/start" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lab_url", "label": "Design Lab link", "default": "https://hub.thefuturebasics.com/join?for=lab" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hero_title", "label": "Hero title" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hero_accent", "label": "Hero title, second line" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "hero_lede", "label": "Hero text" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "marks_label", "label": "Brand list label", "default": "made with" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "min_figure", "label": "Legacy: minimum figure" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "faq_schema", "label": "Add FAQ structured data", "default": true },
    { "type": "select", "id": "part", "label": "Show", "default": "all", "options": [ { "value": "all", "label": "Whole page" }, { "value": "top", "label": "Hero to made by future basics" }, { "value": "end", "label": "Questions and close" } ] }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "mark", "name": "Brand", "settings": [ { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Name" } ] },
    { "type": "figure", "name": "Figure", "settings": [ { "type": "text", "id": "figure", "label": "Figure" }, { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label" } ] },
    { "type": "project", "name": "Project", "settings": [
      { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "client", "label": "Client or brand" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "What it was" },
      { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Short description" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "category", "label": "Category" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "quantity", "label": "Quantity", "info": "e.g. 250 units" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "lead_time", "label": "Lead time", "info": "e.g. 11 weeks" }
    ] },
    { "type": "object", "name": "Category", "settings": [
      { "type": "text", "id": "cap", "label": "Caption" }, { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title" },
      { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Text" }, { "type": "text", "id": "moq", "label": "Minimum and lead time" },
      { "type": "checkbox", "id": "is_note", "label": "Show as a note", "default": false }
    ] },
    { "type": "step", "name": "Step", "settings": [
